on, localization or omitted ancestor is used here.\",\"source_application_check\":\"At R001/S003 M003 is instantiated with the field ℂ, module V, finite nonempty I and family e. F001 supplies card(I)=n>0, F002 establishes independence, and H004 gives dim_ℂ V=λ+1=n. The exact source conclusion is spanning; combining it with F002 yields the basis used next. The factor 2(λ+1-i) in the termination argument is nonzero over ℂ for every i∈I. The source does not supply any string formula; those are proved in S001 and S004.\",\"declaration_check\":\"D001–D004 and D006 introduce n,I,X,Y,e with their full domains; the complex sl₂-module parameters supply the action. The induction variable m is local to S001, and the statement-local t in F001 does not shadow it. The coefficient family c and index j are introduced at S002 and remain only through the independence test. The k in the isolating product and i,r in the universally stated action calculations are formula-bound with the displayed finite ranges. No witnesses from this packet escape except through the complete basis and formula statements in N001.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read R002 using exactly H001,H003,H004,H006,N001,M001,M002,M006. S001 uses admissibility's complex/integer basis and the given dimension to produce F001; it does not assume the standard e_i form a lattice basis. S002 maps the base-changed integer basis into its complex-independent image to prove injectivity and complex spanning. S003 uses the actual generators of U_Z to prove every X_r,Y_r preserves M and then M_R, and obtains h preservation from [x,y]. Its binomial inverse is explicitly j!(λ-j)!/λ!, with all denominator-unit premises established. S004 checks the projection and lowering-string cases before composing the final matrix units. In particular there is no use of reduced distinct weights or a special choice of admissible lattice.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M002 at S001 is over ℂ with the complex basis given by H006; its finite index set follows from the finite-dimensional V of H004, and its cardinality is n. M001 at S002 is the ℤ→R scalar extension of the integer basis chosen from F001; S001 verifies the rational subring, so this is a compatible ℤ-algebra and the source gives the basis 1⊗f_i. M006 at S003 uses ℓ=p and an arbitrary natural t corresponding to 0≤t≤λ; H001 is primality and H003 yields t<p. Coprimality gives p∤t!, so the displayed reciprocal is in R. These conclusions are bridged explicitly to the lattice embedding and unit claims, not merely asserted by the source names.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The integer basis f chosen at S002 has the earlier F001 existence basis and stays in scope through the last use of F002 in S004. D007's prime guard H001 is direct. M_R remains the abstract tensor module until ι_R's injectivity is proved at S002. The coordinate maps E of D010 are used only with direct N001 establishing the complex basis. The action formulas in S004 quantify i,j and test basis indices k within I; all λ-i,λ-j are nonnegative. Neither a common scalar b nor a standard-basis assertion about M is introduced here.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the R003 packet as a conditional theorem with direct N001,N002 and H001, not their producer bodies. N002 supplies the embedding, finite R-basis and all matrix-unit preservation; N001 supplies the complex basis. S001 uses these to prove equality of coordinate modules, finite generation, and both directions and uniqueness of the coordinate decomposition. The temporary zero-module assumption L1 is discharged. S002 proves injection of μ by expressing any tensor as (1/d)⊗c with c∈J; zero image forces c=0. Its displayed tensor generators prove finite generation over ℚ. S003 constructs Φ and its inverse by coordinate maps and finite sums and checks inverse identities on generating simple tensors. S004 therefore legitimately compares dimensions and cancels positive n in n=nr. S005 works under L2:a≠0 and discharges that antecedent before quantifying a,z. No containment-in-ℂ rank shortcut or unproved tensor exactness is used.\",\"source_application_check\":\"In S004 M001 applies to the R-basis of M_R explicitly supplied by N002, with scalar ring ℚ over the subring R. M002 counts the resulting ℚ-basis indexed by the finite I of N001. M007 applies to the ℚ-vector space T constructed in F002 and supplies the freeness premise for M004; F002 separately proves finite generation. M004 then computes the dimension of the constant finite product T^I as nr. M005 uses the actual equivalence Φ of F003 to equate it to dimension n on the other side. In S005 M003 applies to the singleton family 1⊗a in T: under L2 its image μ(1⊗a)=a is nonzero, scalar cancellation proves independence, and F004 gives the singleton dimension equality 1. Its spanning conclusion yields the existential rational coefficient; applying μ gives the claimed equality in ℂ.\",\"declaration_check\":\"D011 and D012 are R-submodules because they are preimages of the R-submodule image of ι_R under the scalar-multiplication maps; this does not assume rank or principality. Direct H001 provides the R guard, and direct N001 provides the E guard. T and μ are explicitly introduced at S002, Φ at S003, and r at S004 after the finite-dimensional assertion F002. Their local ranges include every later use of the corresponding facts. The arbitrary a,z occur only in S005; a's nonzero condition is a discharged local assumption, not its type or an extra H. The finite sums, coefficient tuples and simple-tensor variables in the map formulas are locally quantified in their displayed domains.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read the current R004 packet after the final literal correction. Direct N003, rather than an ancestor basis argument, supplies nonzero finite generation, the rational-line statement and the unique-coordinate decomposition. S001 first proves existence of a nonempty nonzero generating family. S002 then chooses a and g with those grounds, represents their nonzero coefficients in ℚ, and proves the required p-power/unit form by terminating removal of p-factors from nonzero integer numerator and denominator. H001 supplies p≥2; a nonempty finite list has an attained minimum. S003 chooses the compatible exponent/unit/minimizer data from F002 and gives both inclusions J=Rb. It proves spanning and independence of b e_i using exactly N003's unique coordinates and b≠0. No PID classification theorem or assertion that an arbitrary submodule of ℂ has rank one is invoked.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no E/M call in R004. The rational-line statement and module decomposition are explicit direct clauses of N003. The only additional arithmetic construction is displayed in S002: removing prime factors strictly decreases the positive absolute value of a nonzero integer, and the remaining numerator/denominator give mutually inverse elements of R. The finite minimum and differences ν_j-ν≥0 give p^{ν_j-ν}∈R. This proves the principal-generator step locally along the supplied route.\",\"declaration_check\":\"a has direct N003 as its nonzero-witness basis. g is chosen only after the earlier F001 has proved a nonempty generating family exists. F002 quantifies the full families q0,u0,η0, the minimum κ0, the attaining index jmin, and the family index j. At S003 ν,νexp,u,j_0 are explicitly chosen simultaneously from that one existence statement, preserving compatibility. The scalar b is then the explicit expression p^ν a; membership and nonzeroness are proved, not granted by declaration. The corrected S002 no longer uses the later local unit-family name u for its one-rational calculation. All construction witnesses are confined to the inference; N004 exports existential b and the basis property for any such generator.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read R005 with exactly H001,H002,N001,N002,N004,M001,M002. S001 derives denominator invertibility from characteristic, constructs ρ and the first pair of inverse balanced tensor maps. S002 identifies kernel pR and the prime-field image, then verifies quotient-lift independence and balancing for the second tensor identification. S003 chooses b from N004 and proves both the tensor basis and the quotient basis by unique coordinates. S004 uses the now explicit N002 preservation of M by all divided powers, transfers operators through A and B on generating tensors, and retains the complete reduced formulas and nonzero factorial identities. The Chevalley bracket/action identification follows from N002 and preservation of sums and compositions under tensor extension. S005 uses N002's word only after reducing its unit scalar and checks it on the new basis. Under local L1, stability under powers/scalars/compositions proves stability under each matrix unit; L1 is discharged. No extra H006, unexported producer fact or algebraic-closure condition is used.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M001 in S003 uses source ring R, algebra K through the actually constructed ρ, module M_R and the R-basis b e_i supplied by N004. Its native tensor order gives K⊗_R M_R; the proof explicitly supplies the balanced flip and its inverse to reach M_R⊗_R K, and then the already proved isomorphism A^{-1} reaches V(K). M002 counts this transported K-basis; K is a field and hence has strong rank condition, and N001 gives finite I of cardinality n. Nonzero factorials and binomial scalars are not conclusions of these M: they follow from N002's units and the unital map ρ. The resulting scalar multiples are used only at indices 0≤r≤λ.\",\"declaration_check\":\"ρ and A are explicitly defined at S001; B is defined at S002 with the prime-field/quotient structure constructed there. All three remain in scope through S005 because their local facts are reused. The nonzero generator b is chosen from direct N004 at S003, then β is the displayed transported family, and only after F003 proves it a basis are its coordinate maps T introduced in S005. The arbitrary K-subspace W in S005 is not assumed invariant in its type; invariance is L1 and is discharged. D013 gives notation for induced X,Y only after the necessary lattice preservation, now explicitly exported by N002. Private maps and b are used solely to prove the quantified/existential, fully stated N005.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Read R006 from the full statement of N005, H003,H004,H001 and the declared definitions. N005 directly supplies a compatible basis and every coordinate matrix-unit invariance property. H001 is the formation guard for its localization data, H003 gives 0∈I and the endpoint range, and H004 identifies the Chevalley integer span with the L(K) definition. In S001 basis independence proves unconditional nonzeroness F003 before the subspace assumptions. L1 is the invariant-subspace premise; L2 is only the nonzero branch. F001 supplies a nonzero vector, coordinates and index in that branch. In S002 each T_ij produces c_jβ_i, and division is valid because the same chosen coordinate c_j is nonzero in K. Spanning proves W=V(K). L2 closes the case split and L1 closes the implication; S003 universally closes W. The p=2 discussion does not invoke separation of reduced h-eigenvalues.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No E/M is called directly by R006. Its basis, dimension, representation identification and matrix-unit invariance are explicit clauses of direct N005 and are used as conditional premises, not recovered from R005's proof. Invariance under x,y follows from L1, so N005's quantified implication applies to the actual W. The matrix-unit calculation is finite linear algebra using its defining values on β and the displayed coordinates, and field division uses F001's nonzero c_j. H004 and the definition of L(K) show that invariance under the three generators is invariance under their K-span.\",\"declaration_check\":\"β is chosen from N005 at S001; the coordinate family T is defined relative to that same basis. W is arbitrary, with invariant and nonzero assumptions recorded separately as L1 and L2. The simultaneous witnesses w,c,j are introduced at S002 only from earlier F001 and are scoped to the nonzero branch. Their identity does not appear in F002 or P. F003 states the unconditional nonzero conclusion independently of the branch assumptions. H004 is direct for D014's Lie-algebra guard; the interpretation remains the Chevalley construction also in characteristic 2. The final universal conclusion contains no private basis or witness.\"}] }","status":"completed"}}

